# ============================================================================
# 🎯 QUICK START GUIDE
# ============================================================================
# 
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Replace all YOUR_* placeholders with actual values
# 3. Generate secure secrets (see Security Checklist below)
# 4. Never commit .env to version control (already in .gitignore)
# 
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
# 1. Install dependencies: npm install
# 2. Generate Prisma Client: npm run db:generate
# 3. Run migrations: npm run db:migrate
# 4. Seed database (optional): npm run db:seed
# 5. Start development server: npm run start:dev
# 6. Access API: https://mash-backend-api.up.railway.app/api/v1/health
# 7. View API docs: https://mash-backend-api.up.railway.app/api/docs
# 
# RAILWAY DEPLOYMENT (RECOMMENDED):
# 1. Follow: RAILWAY_DEPLOY_NOW.md (complete step-by-step guide)
# 2. Quick reference: docs/RAILWAY_QUICK_START.md
# 3. Use Railway variable references: ${{service-name.VARIABLE_NAME}}
# 4. Example: DATABASE_URL=${{postgres.DATABASE_PRIVATE_URL}}
# 5. Example: REDIS_URL=${{redis.REDIS_PRIVATE_URL}}
# 6. Set all environment variables in Railway dashboard
# 7. Deploy and monitor via Railway logs
# 
# MONITORING & OBSERVABILITY:
# - Prometheus Metrics: https://mash-backend-api.up.railway.app/metrics
# - Grafana Dashboard: http://localhost:3001 (admin/admin123)
# - Jaeger Traces: http://localhost:16686
# - API Health Check: https://mash-backend-api.up.railway.app/api/v1/health
# - WebSocket Connection: ws://localhost:3000/ws
# 
# LOAD TESTING:
# - Windows: .\test\k6\run-all-tests.bat
# - Linux/Mac: ./test/k6/run-all-tests.sh
# - Single test: k6 run test/k6/scenarios/basic-load.js
# 
# ============================================================================
# 🔐 SECURITY CHECKLIST (REQUIRED FOR PRODUCTION)
# ============================================================================
# 
# ⚠️  CRITICAL - Generate Strong Secrets:
# Generate using: openssl rand -hex 32
# 
# [ ] JWT_SECRET - Used for token signing
# [ ] CSRF_SECRET - Used for CSRF protection
# [ ] ENCRYPTION_KEY - Used for data encryption (if implementing)
# [ ] DATABASE_URL - Use strong password, enable SSL
# [ ] REDIS_PASSWORD - Use strong password or managed service
# 
# ⚠️  CRITICAL - Replace All Placeholders:
# [ ] FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID, FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY, etc.
# [ ] EMAIL_USER and EMAIL_PASSWORD (use app-specific password)
# [ ] TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN
# [ ] OPENAI_API_KEY (if using AI features)
# [ ] AWS credentials (if using S3)
# 
# ⚠️  IMPORTANT - Production Settings:
# [ ] NODE_ENV=production
# [ ] LOG_LEVEL=info (not debug)
# [ ] CORS_ORIGINS - Only allow your actual domain(s)
# [ ] Rate limits - Adjust based on expected traffic
# [ ] Database connection pooling enabled
# 
# ✅  RECOMMENDED - Security Features:
# [ ] CSRF_ENABLED=true
# [ ] CACHE_ENABLED=true
# [ ] METRICS_ENABLED=true
# [ ] OTEL_ENABLED=true
# [ ] ANALYTICS_BATCH_ENABLED=true
# 
